# A bug of the prototype (user reports 30.10.2026 and 29.10.2026, 0.95.1, debug discs): the handcannon (item 0x37,
# weapon 0x0F) showed the firepower "0.00" at the merchant, and its exclusive tune-up ("levels 7/1/3/6", 200000
# pesetas) did not give endless ammo. The prototype's WeaponLevelTbl row 0x0F is a placeholder (100.0 on every
# level: x10 with three digits is "0.00"; the damage was 100 times the class value), level_ext_sw500 lifts only
# the firepower to 7, wep_info's capacity level 7 is 0xFFFF (255 rounds after WeaponId2ChargeNum's u8 cast) and no
# code checks for it (trigger, reloadable call WeaponId2ChargeNum and drop the value).
# Read in the European main.dol and Sscrn.rel (retail_code.py, both disc kinds get the fix):
# - WeaponLevelTbl row 0x0F {30, 35, 40, 45, 50, 60, 99.9} (0x8020846c);
# - wep_info 0x34 / 0x37 capacity level 7 = 0x8000 (0x801e3a9c), WeaponId2ChargeNum returns the u16;
# - level_ext_sw500 {0x37, {7, 1, 3, 7}}: the exclusive lifts firepower and capacity (0x801f87c8);
# - capacity 0x8000 is endless: trigger uses no round, reloadable answers 1, reload loads nothing, bulletNum(cItem*)
#   counts 1 for 0x37 / 0x34; the HUD counter (BulletInfo::move), the case (piece numbers, also the endless rocket
#   launcher 0x6D), numDisp, the examine screen and the merchant's levelItemDisp / weaponLevelDisp show the infinity digit 13.
# Not taken over (balance of the final game, no bug): rows 3, 4, 9, 0x11 and 0x2C of WeaponLevelTbl, the chicago
# typewriter's European form (bought with capacity 7 = endless, no exclusive tune-up, reload level 1 at most).
